  "sourceDecisions": [
    "Historical lordships and seats remain despite war and partial occupation. Boyd immediately serves Muirgheal beneath Buadhtreun; Durachd keeps its additional asylum placement.",
    "No invented living heads or blanket extinction of war-damaged houses. Documented survivors remain alive.",
    "Blàthnat Durachd, wife of Oistín Lockart, is alive and born 1698 according to her new origin table; established person/world IDs remain. Oistín died 1725.",
    "Dúrchadh/Durachd variants for Haeghra spouses are reconciled through explicit reciprocal marriages, retaining IDs.",
    "Diarmuid/Diarmaid Diuid, Elewyne/Eleyne Grawn and Jarlaith/Jarlath Drummond preserve canonical IDs and names. Diarmaid death 1704 supplied.",
    "Lomhán and Eilidh death 1720, Veaghán death 1732, and Nóracha/Vaithreach death 1720 fill formerly unknown values from explicit counterpart tables.",
    "Known counterpart dates fill remaining unknown source years; spaced Wuirseach birth 1 7 14 means 1714.",
    "Bochdew-generation note does not specify an additional parentage. Muirgheal remains Dun-Tiarna despite copied Laird wording in succession prose.",
    "Trianach/Isbeil marriage and Trianach/Iúliana affair remain separate. Bardan is the affair child; unknown surnames and template betrothals are not invented."
